    "title": "Crash in Camden County sends 3 people to hospital - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Tom Ignudo ,\n6 hours ago\nWaterford Township crash leaves 3 people injured, police say 00:20\nThree people were injured in a crash in Waterford Township, New Jersey, Wednesday night, police said.\nThe crash happened just before 4:30 p.m. on Jackson Road in the area of Ashland Avenue, according to police.\nPolice said two vehicles were heading eastbound on Jackson Road and went off the side of the road and into a wooded area.\nA vehicle driven by a 59-year-old man with a 60-year-old passenger went off Jackson Road, struck a utility pole and rolled over, according to police. Both the 59-year-old and 60-year-old were from Vincentown, Burlington County, police said.\nThe other vehicle was driven by a 65-year-old man from Browns Mills, Burlington County, according to police. The vehicle went off the road in the crash and came to rest in the wooded area.\nPolice said several people who saw the crash stopped and helped to the three people injured in the accident until first responders arrived.\nThe three people were treated on the scene and airlifted to Cooper University Hospital in Camden, according to police. The conditions for the three people were not immediately available.\nThe crash is under investigation.\n6",
